# viewtest: a frame asked for after the last command round is not lost.  "Kette" queues a
# command; each frame that sees a new link queues the next one, so the click's frame and the next
# two use the three command rounds of run_passes and the third link's change is seen by no frame
# of them: run_passes asks for the next frame (need), which the window loop -- and `wait` -- give.
click "Kette"
wait 16
expect text:"Kette: 3" exists
# again: the same three links, no frame lost the second time either
click "Kette"
wait 16
expect text:"Kette: 3" exists
expect_nowarn
# an app that asks for another frame in every frame (ui.invalidate in App::frame) gets 8 in a
# row, then the frames wait for the next event, with a UIWARN
click "Immer neu"
wait 400
expect_warn
click "Immer neu"
wait 100
expect_nowarn
